{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.ChordDiagram","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.ChordDiagram","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.Perm.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Logic.Equiv.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fintype.Perm","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":21,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.instInhabitedChordDiagramOfNatNat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.instInhabitedChordDiagramOfNatNat","kind":"instance","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Vassiliev/ChordDiagram.lean#L143-L143","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.ChordDiagram.oneChord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.ChordDiagram.oneChord","kind":"def","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Vassiliev/ChordDiagram.lean#L135-L141","doc":"The unique degree-1 chord diagram: the single chord on `Fin 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.ChordDiagram.degree_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.ChordDiagram.degree_conj","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Vassiliev/ChordDiagram.lean#L124-L126","doc":"Conjugation preserves degree (it is always `n`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.ChordDiagram.conj_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.ChordDiagram.conj_mul","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Vassiliev/ChordDiagram.lean#L118-L122","doc":"The relabelling action is a right action of the symmetric group. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.ChordDiagram.conj_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.ChordDiagram.conj_one","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Vassiliev/ChordDiagram.lean#L114-L116","doc":"The identity relabelling fixes a chord diagram. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.ChordDiagram.conj_pairing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.ChordDiagram.conj_pairing","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Vassiliev/ChordDiagram.lean#L111-L112","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.ChordDiagram.conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.ChordDiagram.conj","kind":"def","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Vassiliev/ChordDiagram.lean#L105-L109","doc":"The relabelling action of `g : Perm (Fin (2*n))` on a chord diagram. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.ChordDiagram.fixedPointFree_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.ChordDiagram.fixedPointFree_conj","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Vassiliev/ChordDiagram.lean#L93-L103","doc":"Conjugation preserves fixed-point-freeness. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.ChordDiagram.involutive_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.ChordDiagram.involutive_conj","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Vassiliev/ChordDiagram.lean#L86-L91","doc":"Conjugation preserves involutivity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.ChordDiagram.degree_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.ChordDiagram.degree_eq","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Vassiliev/ChordDiagram.lean#L76-L76","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.ChordDiagram.degree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.ChordDiagram.degree","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Vassiliev/ChordDiagram.lean#L72-L74","doc":"The **degree** of a chord diagram is its number of chords, `= n` by\nconstruction (there are `2 n` endpoints, paired two at a time). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.ChordDiagram.partner_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.ChordDiagram.partner_ne","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Vassiliev/ChordDiagram.lean#L69-L70","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.ChordDiagram.partner_partner","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.ChordDiagram.partner_partner","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Vassiliev/ChordDiagram.lean#L66-L67","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.ChordDiagram.partner","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.ChordDiagram.partner","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Vassiliev/ChordDiagram.lean#L63-L64","doc":"The chord partner of a marked point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.ChordDiagram.ext_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.ChordDiagram.ext_iff","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Vassiliev/ChordDiagram.lean#L60-L60","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.ChordDiagram.ext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.ChordDiagram.ext","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Vassiliev/ChordDiagram.lean#L58-L61","doc":"Two chord diagrams are equal once their pairings agree (the remaining\nfields are propositions, equal by proof irrelevance). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.ChordDiagram.fixedPointFree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.ChordDiagram.fixedPointFree","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Vassiliev/ChordDiagram.lean#L52-L52","doc":"No point is its own partner (every chord has two distinct endpoints). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.ChordDiagram.involutive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.ChordDiagram.involutive","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Vassiliev/ChordDiagram.lean#L50-L50","doc":"The pairing is an involution: applying it twice returns the point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.ChordDiagram.pairing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.ChordDiagram.pairing","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Vassiliev/ChordDiagram.lean#L48-L48","doc":"The pairing permutation: sends each marked point to its chord partner. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.ChordDiagram.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.ChordDiagram.mk","kind":"ctor","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Vassiliev/ChordDiagram.lean#L46-L46","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.ChordDiagram","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.ChordDiagram","kind":"structure","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Vassiliev/ChordDiagram.lean#L42-L52","doc":"A **chord diagram** of degree `n`: a fixed-point-free involution on the\n`2 * n` marked points `Fin (2 * n)`.  `pairing i` is the endpoint joined to\n`i`; involutivity makes the chords well-defined and fixed-point-freeness\nforbids a chord from both ending at the same point. ","signatureChunk":0}]}